WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.310
Inside the nucleus of
your cells is DNA:

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.510
a long molecule made of two
strands, twisted together.

3
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.350
Imagine unzipping it down the middle,

4
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.870
so the two strands come apart.

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.550
Throw one half away.

6
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.110
The half you kept still carries
enough information to rebuild

7
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.650
the missing half exactly.

8
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.870
How can one half know
what the other half said?

9
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.020
In this mission, you'll see the
shape of DNA, a double helix.

10
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.650
You'll meet its four bases,
known by their letters: A, T,

11
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.150
C and G.

12
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.610
And you'll find out how the
order of those bases works as a

13
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.710
code.

14
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.890
Your mission: work out how one
strand of DNA can rebuild the

15
00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:42.750
other.
